<description>
The function `Strnew_m_charp` is a variadic function that takes a variable number of C-style strings and concatenates them into a single `Str` object. The first argument is a C-style string, and the subsequent arguments are also C-style strings, with the list of arguments being terminated by a NULL pointer. The function creates a new `Str` object, and then iterates through the provided C-style strings, concatenating each one to the `Str` object until it encounters a NULL pointer. The callers of this function always pass a NULL pointer as the last argument.
</description>

<requirements>
<requirement>
The variable argument list must be terminated by a NULL pointer. This is because the function iterates through the arguments until a NULL is encountered, and failure to provide one will lead to a crash.
</requirement>
<requirement>
All arguments passed to the function must be valid, null-terminated C-style strings. This is because the function uses `Strcat_charp` which expects null-terminated strings.
</requirement>
</requirements>

